SUMMARY:World Refugee Day Storytelling Event
DESCRIPTION:Support community storytelling and connect with neighbors in the Triangle while listening to true stories at Pour Taproom on June 23rd from 6-8pm. This World Refugee Day event will feature up to 9 storytellers share stories on migration and courage. This event is co-hosted by Flame Tree Story and Story First Design. Flame Tree Story creates spaces where people connect through story–sparking empathy and strengthening community. Story First Design leverages the power of digital learning technologies to bring these stories to life. To learn more\, check out our podcast: https://open.spotify.com/show/1V8mAytdA1FS1ixPzVIZs7?si=98a63951d63a4030
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/world-refugee-day-storytelling-event/
LOCATION:Pour Taproom\, 202 N Corcoran St.\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Cultural,Diversity & Inclusivity,Live Performance,Storytelling
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/World-Refugee-Day-Storytelling-Event_thumbnail.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Flame Tree Story":MAILTO:whitney@flametreestory.com
GEO:35.9964427;-78.9010638
